 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gangs and builds",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Single-gang parts carry one resistive element; dual-gang parts stack two elements, R1 and R2, on one shaft. Dual-gang parts are sold as a tone build (types 122 and 124) or a volume build (types 12B and 12D)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Shaft position",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The flat of the shaft sits at 60° from vertical when the shaft is turned fully counter-clockwise."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Bushing and lug",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The bushing carries an M9×0.75 thread. Below it, with its centre 6 mm from the bushing axis, a lug 2 mm wide and 0.8 mm thick stands 0.8 mm proud of the mounting face."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Accessories",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Each part comes with a hex nut, M9×0.75, 11 mm across flats and 2 mm thick, and a flat washer, ø14 outside, ø9.1 inside, 0.5 mm thick."
  },
  {
